{
 "source": {
  "repository": "OpenPresentation/opf-pptx",
  "commit": "438ce8801701f2fa2531ac56537234d274e36aa7",
  "note": "RR-54: toPptx bytes of chart and table decks that use none of the RR-54 fields (no DataColumn objects, datasets, mapping, source or formats, and only strict-decimal or number chart cells), from main before RR-54 (re-pinned to main 4ca079f, the pptxgenjs-plus 4.3.4 migration of opf-pptx#165, whose output change the owner approved). The RR-54 export must keep these bytes exactly. Regenerate only with an owner decision to change the default export. FA-03: the stacked and percent-stacked entries name the clean chart type ids (no -3x suffix), so their titles and tags, and so their bytes, changed; every other entry is unchanged. FA-23 (OPF 0.15, owner-approved breaking spec): every entry regenerated: with zero built-in catalog records the engine-default colour scheme is written as clrScheme name=\"OpenPresentation\" (0.14 named the built-in cool-horizon record \"Cool Horizon\"), and chartex-native-map names the world chart type, since map is no 0.15 chart type. Generated on the FA-20 + FA-22 core branches with zero built-ins; re-run at integration with the released core 0.15. RR-59: the three entries with a table (table, styled-table, mixed-blocks) are repinned because full provenance now records every inline table as authored (the OPF_DATA_V1 tag); previousSha256 keeps the FA-23 hash and nativeSlideSha256 locks the slide XML without its customer-data tags, which is unchanged. RR-59 (AUTO-18, round trip restores absent document defaults): full provenance now records the document-level defaults a document leaves to the engine (OPF_DOCUMENT_V1.absent), so every full-mode export carries the document tag and its slide tags, also when the document states nothing else. Verified part by part against a build of main 3d2698f: with the OPF_DOCUMENT_V1 and OPF_SLIDE_V1 tag parts, their relationships, content-type overrides and custDataLst references removed, every package is byte-identical to main; only the tag parts changed. opf-pptx#175 (chart series in ECMA-376 schema order): the six entries with a line, radar or scatter chart (line, radar, scatter, scatter-two-columns, scatter-labels, mixed-blocks) are repinned because their chart part changed: line series write c:marker before c:dLbls (CT_LineSer), radar series drop the bar-only c:invertIfNegative (CT_RadarSer), and the scatter X c:valAx drops the category-axis-only c:auto, c:lblAlgn and c:noMultiLvlLbl (CT_ValAx). Verified part by part against a build of main d7ae170: ppt/charts/chart1.xml is the only changed part of each package; every other entry is byte-identical. previousSha256 of those six entries is their main d7ae170 hash (mixed-blocks: its FA-23 hash was c5617168f7ff0601b401c939e0d174f70586d02ea0f7268bd36e491398f2eb75); nativeSlideSha256 is unchanged. RR-81: explicit owner-authorized OPF 0.19 default-export update (design section 8), independently reviewed before repinning. Baseline converter 991023c, core fe9fe3fa2c3ad0130e271b73d9853f66e920c1d5, renderer 9fbddcb78dbebcb87355922ca92af7d26c24c48d, Node 24.21.0. All 21 archives add OPF auto titleOnly layout/relation/tag and registrations. Every changed slide XML differs only by native title placeholder and noGrp locks. Chart parts, chart relationships, workbooks, embeddings, themes and diagnostics are unchanged. Three native-slide hashes intentionally reflect those title bindings. Previous RR-81 hashes are retained. Archive acceptance is not native raster acceptance. RR-20 (OPF 0.19 area arrays): approved source-derived archive refresh against frozen core 8f70cf1b52dc4ca4eb246a6f9d065b1403edbf31, gallery 146e477196405fe7d2283008f6fad34c12742599 and candidate PPTX converter. The prior RR-54 SHA is retained in rr20PreviousSha256. Independent 21-case proof: historical published source reproduces all 21 archived bytes under either preserved or new coherent core/gallery graph; 19 candidate archives change, pie and doughnut remain byte-identical. All ZIP part sets/counts are identical; chart parts differ only by neutral 3AC67A to 475569 and four zero-domain minima; table slides only by neutral borders and authored numeric right alignment. Chart/workbook data, slide text and OPF authored data are unchanged. OPF data tags only update evidence hashes and slide tags only native.style hashes. Review receipt: docs/evidence/rr20-array-areas/rr54-archive-review.json. This archive acceptance is not native raster acceptance. RR-20 row-data provenance: independently reviewed and approved update of only single-column against baseline converter e673f106c2fd38fcb5d51db190649c3855cc1885. Adds OPF_DATA_V1 for an authored single column actually plotted against synthetic row numbers. Only that tag, its content-type override, slide relationship and customer-data link change; every native part and all other archives remain byte-identical. Prior hash and size are retained; evidence: docs/evidence/rr20-row-data-provenance/archive-review.json. Native raster acceptance remains separate. Regenerated for RR-94 (tag parts only: text-shape fingerprints and OPF_IMAGE_V1 on every image block). Regenerated for RR-90 (opf-pptx 0.22.1): chart text is core chartTextSize, so chart part text sizes changed.",
  "rr20RowDataReview": {
   "baselineConverter": "e673f106c2fd38fcb5d51db190649c3855cc1885",
   "runtime": "Node 24.21.0",
   "changedEntry": "single-column",
